 \textbf{Cross-Dialect Seed Transfer.} To address seed scarcity for emerging DBMS testing, cross-DBMS SQL transfer has emerged as an active research direction~\cite{zhou2020database}, but this is challenging due to SQL dialect differences.
 As shown in Table~\ref{tab:translation-capability}, existing tools provide limited support for preserving cross-statement dependencies during test-case-level transfer for fuzzing.
 Specifically, existing SQL translation techniques~\cite{sqlglot, jooq} primarily focus on statement-level translation. In contrast, fuzzing seeds are multi-statement test cases that include complex interactions among DDL, DML, and DQL statements.
-\sedar{}~\cite{fu2024sedar} transfers complete test cases, but it does not maintain translated target-side context across statements and leaves target-side execution-feedback regeneration as future work. \tool{} instead explicitly represents test structures and forward read-after-write dependencies in an AQT, coordinates instantiation with evolving target-side schema and type context, and uses parser and execution feedback to repair transferred seeds before downstream mutation.
